    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302">

                <pb facs="0377" n="359" xml:id="pg359"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/7–2146: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Flack</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1946-07-21T12:10:00-04:00"
                            notBefore="1946-07-19T11:00:00-04:00">undated</date>.<lb/>[Received July
                        21, 1946—12:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Unnumbered. Attention Byrnes. Anarchy has broken loose in La Paz. Students and
                    public have secured guns and ammunition from Municipal Palace and have attacked
                    and taken traffic headquarters. No evidence of soldiers or police in streets.
                    Please inform War and Justice Departments.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d302-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Flack</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d302-f1" n="36" xml:id="d302-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram 684, July 21, 1946, the Ambassador reported that a Junta
                    Institutional had taken over the Government (824.00/7–2146).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
